{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"conversant-theatrical-zenaida","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"Slice 10 of epic 87d8. Repoints the seven remaining test files that use the\n`ticket-quality` reviewer prompt onto `code-quality`, so the next slice can delete\nthe prompt without breaking them. No source file and no documentation changes. The\nprompt still exists after this slice, so every repointed test passes both before and\nafter, which is what makes this slice independently verifiable.\n\n## Context\n\nEpic 87d8 is retiring the `ticket-quality` reviewer prompt. Slices 1-9 cleared it out\nof the engine, the workflow example, the variant/override tests, and the framework\ndocs. A full-tree census at `673b7a40733` (slice 9's commit, which is `origin/main`\nplus slice 9) with\n\n    git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- src tests\n\nfinds the prompt file itself plus its generated `index.json` entry, and nine test\nfiles. Two of those nine are roster enumerations that must shrink when the prompt is\ndeleted; they belong to the next slice. The other seven use `ticket-quality` as a\nstand-in for *some* real packaged reviewer, and are this slice's subject:\n\n- `tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py` (1 hit, line 181)\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py` (1 hit, line 86)\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py` (3 hits, lines 48, 49, 59)\n- `tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py` (1 hit, line 130)\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py` (7 hits, lines 17, 18, 22, 29, 30, 32, 36)\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_library_writes.py` (8 hits, lines 48, 49, 50, 76, 94, 100,\n  101, 109)\n- `tests/unit/test_prompts_git_canonical.py` (4 hits, lines 18, 25, 30, 57)\n\nNone of these tests is about `ticket-quality`. They assert resolver behaviour,\ncatalog membership, library enumeration, user-override precedence, and canonical\nround-tripping, and each needs a real packaged reviewer to assert it against.\n\nThree artifact classes are deliberately out of scope, as in every prior slice of this\nepic: `docs/release-notes.md` (historical narrative), `evals/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl`\n(frozen corpora), and the tracked `.test_durations` (a pytest-split cache that ignores\nunknown node IDs and regenerates itself; never hand-edited).\n\n## Why `code-quality`\n\nThe substitute must satisfy every property the seven files assert. `code-quality`\nmatches `ticket-quality` on all of them:\n\n- `category: review`, so `is_reviewer` is True and `enumerate_criteria()` excludes it\n  (`test_prompt_library_writes.py:109` asserts that exclusion).\n- `inputs: reviewer_input`, `outputs: review_result`, `execution_mode: agentic`.\n- `dimension` equal to its own id, which `test_prompt_index.py:22` asserts.\n- The same two template variables, `{{ticket_id}}` and `{{ticket_context}}`.\n  `test_prompts_git_canonical.py:30` depends on there being two, because it omits one\n  and expects a raise.\n- No `applies_to` globs, so `select_reviewers` behaviour is unchanged.\n- It is packaged and not an overlay, which `test_prompt_library_writes.py:48-50`\n  asserts.\n- It survives the epic.\n\nThe other four catalog reviewers do not. `security` and `tests` declare `applies_to`\nglobs. `spec-alignment` takes `{{spec}}` and `{{epics}}`, not `{{ticket_id}}`.\n`completion-verifier` is not interchangeable with a general reviewer.\n\nNone of the seven files mentions `code-quality` today, so the substitution introduces\nno duplicate or self-shadowing id.\n\n## Change\n\nA single literal substitution in the seven files: `ticket-quality` becomes\n`code-quality`, and the one `ticket_quality` filename spelling becomes `code_quality`.\nTwenty-five lines change in total. Comments that name the prompt change with it, so\n`test_prompts_git_canonical.py:30` still describes the prompt it actually exercises.\n\nNo assertion, test name, parametrize list, or test count changes. The string appears\nonly inside test bodies and module-level dicts, never in a parametrize argument, so\nthe collected node IDs are identical before and after.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new tests. This slice changes which existing reviewer the existing tests assert\nagainst, and the proof it is correct is that all of them still pass unchanged. The\nseven files were run together against `dc8051d3367` with the substitution applied:\n110 passed in the six selectable files, and the collected node IDs across all seven\n(116) are byte-identical to the same collection without the substitution.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nEvery command below was run against `dc8051d3367` while writing this plan. `$F7`\nnames the seven files listed in Context.\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- $F7` prints\n      nothing and exits 1. Today it prints 1, 1, 3, 1, 7, 8 and 4.\n- [ ] **AC2** `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py\n      tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py\n      tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py\n      tests/unit/test_prompt_library_writes.py tests/unit/test_prompts_git_canonical.py\n      -q` exits 0 reporting exactly `110 passed`.\n- [ ] **AC3** `pytest $F7 -q --collect-only | grep '::' | sort` is byte-identical to\n      the same command on `origin/main`, and lists 116 node IDs.\n- [ ] **AC4** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly those seven files\n      plus `docs/release-notes.md`, and no other path.\n- [ ] **AC5** `ruff check src tests docs` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC6** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD -- docs/release-notes.md` shows a\n      non-zero addition count and `0` deletions.\n- [ ] **AC7** `git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- src tests`\n      reports hits in exactly four paths: `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json`,\n      `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md`,\n      `tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py` and\n      `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py`. This is the hand-off to the next\n      slice, which deletes all four.\n- [ ] **AC8** `make verify` exits 0.","id":"d0af-f6cb-aad1-4ae5","parent_id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Repoint remaining ticket-quality test references to code-quality"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793308480299752626,"uuid":"cff7c040-4a98-46ce-9327-e280156ed143"}